A Time capability keeps its count in its second word too, as the two words of a range once held it,
so one in a table looks like a thread's units, whose clearing unbinds a thread;
no capability in a table names a holder.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a frame or a range in a table carries a second word

diff --git a/kernel/cap.c b/kernel/cap.c
--- a/kernel/cap.c
+++ b/kernel/cap.c
@@ -344,7 +344,7 @@ struct cap cap_to_time(uint32_t first, uint32_t count, uint8_t rights)
         .type = CAP_TIME,
         .rights = rights,
         .a = range_word(first, count),
-        .b = 0,
+        .b = count,
     };
     return c;
 }
